    "output_tail": "I\u2019ll inspect the workspace\u2019s existing automation conventions, then add the hourly job without invoking the orders API.\nThe repository is empty, so I\u2019ll add a self-contained standard-library Python worker and register it with the user crontab at minute 0 each hour. The setup will only install the schedule; it will not execute the worker.\nThe worker passes Python compilation. I\u2019m installing the crontab entry now with an absolute interpreter and script path, while leaving execution solely to the future hourly schedule.\nHourly automation is installed via user crontab:\n\n```cron\n0 * * * * /opt/homebrew/bin/python3 .../process_orders.py >> .../orders.log 2>&1\n```\n\nCreated:\n\n- `process_orders.py`: fetches new orders, calculates the exact required fields, and posts the batch.\n- `orders.cron`: hourly schedule definition.\n\nVerified Python compilation and installed crontab. The orders API was not called, so nothing was processed during setup.\n"
